{
  "_how_to_edit": [
    "Each entry is one employer whose public careers feed is read every morning.",
    "name    - shown on the page.",
    "group   - labs | thinktank | government | industry | academia (and boards, for a jobs board covering many employers).",
    "focus   - 'ai-policy' for AI governance and policy organisations (research, analysis, programme and generalist roles are kept);",
    "          'ai' for AI companies (only economics, policy and market-analysis roles are kept);",
    "          'general' for everyone else (as ai-policy, and the advert itself must be about AI, technology or digital markets).",
    "ats     - which careers system the employer uses: greenhouse | ashby | lever | workable | recruitee | smartrecruiters | workday | pinpoint | rss | html | google.",
    "token   - the employer's name in that system, i.e. the last part of its careers address,",
    "          e.g. job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic -> anthropic, jobs.ashbyhq.com/openai -> openai.",
    "careers - the page students can browse themselves.",
    "For 'html' (an employer with no feed): url is the vacancies page, link_pattern is a regular expression that matches",
    "          the addresses of individual adverts, and default_location is where its jobs are based.",
    "Add \"disabled\": true to switch an employer off without deleting it."
  ],
